we here at maxtech have used quite a few  projectors before but never anything  like these new portable laser projectors  sent to us from our sponsor nebula the  capsule 3 laser which is battery powered  and the cosmos laser 4K which has  incredible HDR so to give both of these  a proper review with all of our thoughts  and suggestions I went ahead and took  the smaller one home to test out with my  family and let me tell you right now I  was blown away by the quality the  brightness the battery life the  smoothness of the UI and more and then  Max took the cosmos home to his legit  home theater with a huge projector  screen so he's going to be sharing his  thoughts and reviewing this one but  first I've got to talk about the capsule  3 laser because it honestly blew me away  being by far the best projector I've  seen or tested for multiple reasons  first of all this thing is Tiny it's  literally smaller than the coffee I got  this morning check that out you could  probably fit this thing in your pocket  you know what let's do a test right here  on camera yep it fits it fits in my  pocket but the crazy thing is that you  don't need anything to set it up because  it's basically a smart TV built into a  portable projector with Android TV 11  which works great and I'll get into that  in just a minute now the first time I  tested this thing out I set it up  against the inside of a donut box and  started streaming movies from basically  any streaming platform like Netflix HBO  Max Amazon Prime or Apple TV plus but  what really blew my mind about it was  that it was that bright thanks to it  being a laser projector and not LED like  others on the market and all while being  completely battery powered yes it has  2.5 hours of battery life which is  basically enough for most movies out  there and that's due to its laser engine  technology being 1.8 times brighter than  LED at the same wattage now I tested it  out in multiple locations like at my  mother-in-law's house in the basement  using their projector screen in my own  living room against a quick hanging  sheet solution over my fireplace and I  even took it outside and set it up  against my white vinyl fence for a big  screen experience with some blankets and  surprisingly even though our Wi-Fi  connection is terrible outside I was  able to connect it with no issues at all  with no buffering while streaming some  cartoons on YouTube and I love that the  included remote has a little autofocus  and auto Keystone button that you simply  press to refocus if it was bumped or  moved without needing to go up to it and  manually adjust it in a nice little  inclusion is a little mount on the  bottom so you can set it up on a tripod  for a more stable and higher up Solution  on the back you'll find an HDMI 2.1 Port  which is really nice and a USBC port for  either charging or even for connecting  media and an auxiliary port if you want  to Output the audio to a speaker system  but the one thing that shocked me the  most was the built-in 8 watt speaker  that not only got crazy loud but the  quality was also really good with a  Dolby Digital plus certification just  hear it for yourself if we want to go  fast we need to transform  I know we can be high speed  so because that great sound quality it  also doubles as a Bluetooth speaker with  10 plus hours of battery life simply  press this button on the back to go into  Bluetooth speaker mode and connect to it  now the image quality itself was  actually incredible with 1080p  resolution and very impressive contrast  and color reproduction with HDR 10 plus  certification which looks great and you  can even expand out to a full  150 inch projector screen which is  massive and finally the last piece of  the puzzle is the software and UI  because if it doesn't work well it'll  ruin the entire experience but  thankfully the Android TV 11 software  was very nice and responsive with no  issues at all along with a ton of  different apps on the App Store to  choose from and I was pleasantly  surprised by the remote and how reliable  it was and as the last little cherry on  top if you forget the remote the capsule  3 user comes with touch controls on the  top with navigation buttons volume and a  back button as well so after using it  for a while I've realized that this is  basically the best all-around projector  I could ever imagine due to the  combination of the portability the fact  that it's battery powered the speaker  quality the laser image quality and the  UI basically making it a killer TV  replacement for people like me who don't  actually want a TV in their house now  with that said let's move over to Max  for his review of the cosmos laser 4K  before I get into the differences  between the two now I do have multiple  TVs in my house as well as a theater  room which I've dreamed about for over a  decade I love Cinema and I'm so blessed  to be able to have a setup that our  family can enjoy without having to go  out to the theaters now when I set this  up just a year ago I looked into laser  projectors but they were so expensive  that I settled on a regular DLP 4K  projector that was really well rated by  but now nebula released this 4K  projector which is not only laser but it  is also portable with the handle built  into it as far as physical connections  you have an AUX a USB HDMI and the power  connector and you get a 4K Android TV  that pops into a hidden slot in the back  which means that you could theoretically  swap it out in the future now it  supports everything including Netflix  which my projector doesn't for some  reason you get a Smart Remote as well as  physical controls on the top or you can  just use their app which is very  convenient now I was blown away by the  image especially when you consider the  price my 4K projector like I said it's  really well rated but an issue with  projectors is that blacks look great and  the highlights don't pop much even with  HDR this is where the nebula Cosmos 4K  blew me away now you can't see the full  difference recorded by a camera through  YouTube's compression but the contrast  is better with blacks look looking more  black and Shadow details having more  gradation and separation what's even  crazier are the highlights which blew my  mind once I saw those first lightning  bolts blasting across my screen they are  much brighter and actually look like  true HDR from a really really good TV  compared to my DLP projector which still  looks flat even though it is technically  HDR the difference is massive not only  that but the color reproduction is  amazing with the laser projector just  look at the difference in colors with  the HDR image it is not only saturation  or the brightness of the color but the  actual usable color range like in this  flower shot where my DLP projector looks  mostly purple but the laser has a wide  gradient of colors now the biggest  Nemesis two projectors is ambient  lighting which turns a good image to a  super washed out one as you guys could  see the nebula isn't rated any brighter  than my good 4K project injector but  with ambient lighting you could still  see A Brighter Image with the brights  popping more and better colors as well  so why is it such a big difference well  with the standard projector you have one  lamp that shines white light and then  has to make color out of that whereas  here we have three lasers that output  more light and color resulting in a  brighter more contrasty and more Vivid  and color accurate image the way that  the filmmakers intended and get this the  price of the nebula Cosmos 4K laser  projector is practically the same as my  projector which is why it is so special  since other laser projectors are much  much more expensive so you cannot get a  better image for the price than with  this it's also portable and it has a 30  watt speaker system with two mid drivers  that deliver surprising bass as well as  two tweeters for the highs overall the  nebula Cosmos 4K performed way better  than I expected and now I'll be  replacing my DLP projector knowing just  how much better the image looks in every  way and now if you're wondering what's  different between these two nebula  projectors the biggest difference is  obviously the portability and the fact  that the capsule 3 laser is battery  powered offering more flexibility the  cosmos laser 4K is also much heavier  being 10.7 pounds instead of only around  2 pounds on the capsule and it's also  quite a bit more expensive at twenty two  hundred dollars compared to a hundred  dollars retail for the capsule 3 laser  so basically the cosmos is meant for the  high-end use cases where you can still  take it with you on the go while the  capsule 3 laser is more for the common  family or person who wants not only a  high quality projector but a smart one  with Android TV that's incredibly easy  to set up and put away with really good  built-in speakers and one that you can  take anywhere with no wires thanks to it  being battery powered so once again  thank you nebula for sponsoring this  review and if you're interested in  either of these two laser projectors  you'll find lace of them down below in  the description and pin comment thanks  for watching and we'll see you in the  next video
 

